ns and investments, linking financial considerations with service quality and the student experience. Responsibilities Support the Real Estate, IT and Campus Life departments in their budgeting, forecasting and investment decisions. Build business cases and financial models for real estate and technology projects, and monitor their ROI. Monitor budget execution, commitments, cash outflows and project costs across multiple campuses. Develop indicators combining financial data, service usage and student satisfaction. Produce analyses for Senior Management and contribute to decision-making and resource allocation. Harmonise practices and improve reporting, business intelligence and data analytics tools. Profile required Required Skills and Experience Degree in finance from a leading business or engineering school or university. 5 to 10 years’ experience in management control within a demanding environment, a Big Four audit firm or transaction services. Excellent skills in management control, financial analysis and financial modelling. Proven experience in business partnering is essential; international and matrix-environment experience is desirable. Ability to communicate complex information, formulate recommendations and support decision-making. Ability to organise one’s workload and priorities, demonstrate initiative and work rigorously. Fluent professional English and excellent understanding of financial issues. Interest in investments, real estate and transformation projects within an international environment. Required languages English - Level Bilingual Réf: 98f9405b-b33d-493d-8c6c-453fb2486569 Apply European Financial Controller – Infrastructure and Campus Life F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 