ogrammes and provides the analyses required to support strategic decisions, with the aim of optimising resources and ensuring the sustainability of the academic model. Responsibilities Prepare, consolidate and monitor the budgets and forecasts of the Initial Education BU across all campuses. Produce monthly reports, analyse variances and provide operational recommendations. Define and monitor key financial indicators, including cost per student, programme profitability and campus contribution. Support Programme Management and Academic Management in their financial forecasts and decision-making, including the analysis of options relating to the development of specialisations and programmes, locations, etc. Build financial models and business plans for new programmes and academic projects. Coordinate financial processes across campuses and ensure the reliability of data and reporting. Develop financial monitoring tools and contribute to cross-functional projects related to ERP systems, business intelligence, planning and data. Profile required Required Skills and Experience Degree in finance from a leading business or engineering school or university. 5 to 8 years’ experience in management control within a demanding environment, transaction services or a Big Four audit firm. Proven experience in business partnering is essential; international and matrix-environment experience is desirable. Excellent knowledge of management control, financial modelling, Excel and BI tools; knowledge of an ERP system is a plus. Excellent command of professional English and of financial and accounting terminology, particularly IFRS standards. Ability to produce structured financial analyses and implement the necessary actions to achieve objectives. Ability to engage with non-financial stakeholders, present complex information and formulate recommendations. Ability to organise one’s workload, set priorities and manage responsibilities independently in a multi-campus environment. Ability to demonstrate initiative and propose solutions tailored to the challenges encountered. Required languages English - Level Bilingual Réf: aed00a7a-07e2-4f2d-b468-979690dead08 Apply European Financial Controller – Initial Education BU F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Quelles sont vos motivations pour rejoindre ESCP Business school Quelle est votre compréhension du poste que nous proposons ? * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best pract