    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/internships-officer-094cac": {
      "title": "Internships officer F/H",
      "description": "Internships officer F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Internships officer F/H Apply to this job Internships officer F/H I apply Published on               \n                24/09/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Within ESCP Business School’s Internships Department, the successful candidate manages the administrative processes related to internships and professional experiences in compliance with applicable regulations. The role serves as the key point of reference for a dedicated academic programme and develops in-depth knowledge of its specific requirements, schedule and priorities. Key responsibilities Internship administration Prepare internship agreements governed by French law. Monitor, review, accept and validate professional experience records, including internship agreements and other types of contracts. Respond to questions from students, companies and internal departments regarding French internship legislation. Participate in workshops and forums, in both English and French, to present the department, JobTeaser, programme requirements and French internship legislation. Coordinate student profiles with the academic administration teams of the different programmes. Report any issues, delays or situations requiring escalation to the Head of the Internships Unit and seek support from the person responsible for coordination to further develop operational skills. Dedicated academic programme Take responsibility for a specific academic programme and develop in-depth knowledge of it in order to provide support tailored to the programme and the specific needs of its students. Develop detailed knowledge of the programme’s specific requirements, schedule, key milestones and priorities. Act as the main point of contact for academic administration teams, students and partner companies regarding the assigned programme. Profile required A two- or three-year higher education degree (Bac +2/3) or equivalent; initial experience in an intercultural environment ( more than 60% of the student population is international ) would be an advantage. Ability to organise workload and determine priorities , a strong service mindset, ability to work as part of a team, and attention to the quality and reliability of the work delivered. Strong interpersonal skills and a focus on supporting different audiences. Interest in and confidence using digital tools and information systems. Excellent command of both French and English, written and spoken, as the role involves regular communication in both languages. Proficiency in Chinese (Mandarin) would be an advantage, given the student and corporate audiences supported. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 094cac9b-145a-4631-87ef-ae2c25871577 Apply Internships officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Pourquoi souhaitez vous rejoindre ESCP Business School ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee aw