    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/market-intelligence-manager-2a400f": {
      "title": "Market Intelligence Manager F/H",
      "description": "Market Intelligence Manager F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Market Intelligence Manager F/H Apply to this job Market Intelligence Manager F/H I apply Published on               \n                19/10/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Within the Careers Centre at ESCP Business School, the successful candidate will contribute to enhancing students’ employability and career success by developing a deeper understanding of job markets, companies and recruitment practices. Combining Market Intelligence, Business Insights and data analysis, this role aims to turn information from multiple sources into actionable insights, resources and recommendations. These insights will help Careers Centre teams anticipate market developments and strengthen the support provided to students throughout their internship and job searches. Key Responsibilities : Market Intelligence & Insights – 70% Develop and structure knowledge of employment markets, industries, companies and recruitment practices. Collect, consolidate and analyse information from various internal and external sources to identify trends and career opportunities. Build and engage a network of alumni, industry professionals and subject-matter experts to deepen the understanding of professions and employment markets. Collaborate with Careers teams across ESCP's European campuses to encourage knowledge sharing and make effective use of market insights. Turn collected information into actionable analyses, resources and recommendations to better prepare students for recruitment processes. Identify and propose initiatives to strengthen team expertise and improve the effectiveness of career support services. Data Quality & Business Insights – 30% Contribute to ensuring the quality, reliability and consistency of data related to Careers Centre activities. Support the harmonisation of practices and continuous improvement of data quality. Collaborate with the School's Data & Business Intelligence teams on performance indicators and decision-support tools. Analyse activity data and student feedback to identify trends, needs and opportunities for improvement. Produce and share analyses and recommendations to support decision-making and improve the outcomes of initiatives. Profile required The role is open to candidates with a higher education degree and 5 to 8 years of experience in Market Intelligence, Business Insights, Knowledge Management, Talent Intelligence, consulting or strategic analysis. We are looking for candidates who combine a strong understanding of business challenges with a genuine interest in data. The ability to analyse and structure information from multiple sources, identify key insights and translate them into actionable recommendations is essential. Key skills and qualities include: Excellent analytical, synthesis and information-structuring skills; Strong curiosity about markets, companies and career paths; Confidence in working with data and using it to support decision-making; Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to develop networks of contributors; Ability to work in project-based environments with multiple stakeholders; Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and ability to take initiative; Ability to work effectively in a cross-functional and international environment. An excellent command of English is essential. Knowledge of recruitment, employment markets or employability-related challenges would be an advantage. Réf: 2a400f0d-a44c-4c87-8716-8ff382a27c08 Apply Market Intelligence Manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Pourquoi souhaitez vous rejoindre ESCP Business School ? * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Finance Order-to-Cash and Sales Administration Coordinator F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Market Intelligence Manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Accreditation Officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 5 months Full time London I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
