      "title": "Accreditation Officer F/H",
      "description": "Accreditation Officer F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Accreditation Officer F/H Apply to this job Accreditation Officer F/H I apply Published on               \n                19/10/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Within the Rankings, Strategic Studies, Accreditations and Quality Department, the Accreditation Officer is responsible for the operational implementation of the institution’s and its degree programmes’ recognition, assessment and continuous improvement processes. The role covers French and international accreditations and recognitions in higher education. It requires an excellent understanding of the French quality assurance environment, particularly the requirements of HCERES, Qualiopi and the RNCP and, more broadly, the stakeholders and obligations relating to initial education, apprenticeships and continuing education. 1. Lead the implementation of accreditation processes Monitor the renewal schedule for accreditations and degree recognitions. Organise data collection from the various departments, analyse the data and integrate it into the tables and formats required by the relevant standards. Ensure the traceability of decisions, data, requests for clarification and approvals. Contribute to the preparation of the School’s self-assessment files and reports (HCERES, RNCP, EQUIS, AACSB, etc.), as well as degree recognition files (EFMD Accredited, etc.). Organise and monitor the School’s quality approach based on the Qualiopi standard, in coordination with the relevant departments. Prepare and organise audit visits with the various departments concerned. 2. Coordinate institutional surveys Coordinate data collection from the relevant departments and centralise responses. Complete additional annual quantitative and qualitative surveys (CGE, Onisep, etc.), ensuring consistency with the data submitted to accreditation bodies. 3. Monitor developments Monitor changes in standards, regulations, assessment and certification criteria, as well as practices in higher education institutions. Monitor developments in the accreditation environment and in labels relevant to the School. Contribute to preparing internal or external information on quality and accreditation processes, in coordination with the relevant departments. Profile required Education and experience Master’s degree (Bac+5) in management, project management, quality, higher education, law, administration or a related field. Four to five years’ experience in a similar operational role involving coordination, quality, accreditation, compliance, reporting or project management in higher education, vocational training or an environment subject to compliance requirements is expected. Practical experience preparing files and audits, maintaining monitoring dashboards or managing documentation in a Grande École is a significant advantage. Technical skills Good knowledge of the French higher education environment, its main stakeholders and its quality standards, particularly HCERES, Qualiopi, RNCP and France Compétences. Good knowledge of international accreditations (AACSB, EQUIS, EFMD). Ability to read a standard, identify its requirements and translate them into actions, evidence and deliverables. Excellent command of Excel or an equivalent tool for data consolidation, monitoring dashboards and reporting. Excellent writing, summarising, structuring and document-formatting skills. Proficiency in office and collaborative tools, shared workspaces and document management procedures. Professional English enabling the candidate to read, write and communicate with international organisations. Personal qualities Strong execution skills, attention to detail, responsiveness and reliability. Organisation, forward planning and the ability to manage several schedules simultaneously. Autonomy in task monitoring and persistence in follow-ups. Strong interpersonal skills, a service-oriented approach and the ability to work cross-functionally. Discretion, respect for confidentiality and a strong focus on data quality. Ability to deliver tangible results within tight deadlines. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: a5078f11-ccb4-46e3-ac8a-6564bfca2db4 Apply Accreditation Officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Quelles sont vos motivations pour rejoindre ESCP Business school Quelle est votre compréhension du poste que nous proposons ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Finance Order-to-Cash and Sales Administration Coordinator F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Market Intelligence Manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Accreditation Officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 5 months Full time London I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
